From 3752b7de22b5a1e8af16f9c45b69e548fc2da2b2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Doctor Logix <doctor.logix@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 22:34:14 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] ipa: simple: Estimate white balance from grey zones

The software ISP only reports whole-frame colour sums, so a large coloured
area moves the white balance: under a cool lamp, a green aquarium filling
the frame left a white wall blue.

Add a 16x12 grid of colour sums to the software statistics, leaving out
samples with a saturated channel. When the tuning file gives an illuminant
locus, estimate the illuminant only from the zones whose colour lies close
to it, and fall back to the whole-frame average when none does.

Extend the IMX890 locus with the stock High CCT point, assumed at 10000 K.
